    skos:definition "an alkali of commerce obtained by the combustion of sea-weeds. British barilla is the crude soda-ash left from common salt in the carbonate of soda manufactories; a Spanish name for copper-ore in dust. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 38]"@en ;
